Looking at your code, I can see the issue. The problem is in the dataValidator.sanitizeInput function - it's converting apostrophes and other characters to HTML entities (&#x27;, &quot;, &#x2F;). These entities contain ampersands (&), which are causing the weird characters in your PDF.

Here's the simple fix - modify the sanitizeInput function. Find this code (around line 950-960):

```javascript
sanitizeInput: function(input) {
    // Basic XSS protection
    if (typeof input === 'string') {
        return input
            .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
            .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
            .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
            .replace(/'/g, '&#x27;')
            .replace(/\//g, '&#x2F;');
    }
    return input;
},
```

Replace it with this:

```javascript
sanitizeInput: function(input) {
    // Basic XSS protection - minimal escaping only
    if (typeof input === 'string') {
        return input
            .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
            .replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
    }
    return input;
},
```

Then run this function once in your browser console (F12) to fix existing corrupted data:

```javascript
function fixExistingMaintenanceData() {
    let maintenance = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('maintenance') || '[]');
    let changed = false;
    
    for (let i = 0; i < maintenance.length; i++) {
        if (maintenance[i].activity) {
            let original = maintenance[i].activity;
            let fixed = original
                .replace(/&#x27;/g, "'")
                .replace(/&quot;/g, '"')
                .replace(/&#x2F;/g, '/')
                .replace(/&amp;/g, '&')
                .replace(/&lt;/g, '<')
                .replace(/&gt;/g, '>');
            
            if (fixed !== original) {
                maintenance[i].activity = fixed;
                changed = true;
                console.log('Fixed:', original, '→', fixed);
            }
        }
    }
    
    if (changed) {
        localStorage.setItem('maintenance', JSON.stringify(maintenance));
        alert('Fixed corrupted data! Refresh the page.');
        location.reload();
    } else {
        alert('No corrupted data found. Try adding a new maintenance task - it should work correctly now.');
    }
}

fixExistingMaintenanceData();
```

What's happening:

1. The old sanitizeInput function was converting apostrophes ' to &#x27; (which contains &)
2. These & symbols were being stored in localStorage
3. When the PDF tried to display them, they appeared as & &P&o&s&t...

After this fix:

· New maintenance tasks will be saved correctly (no HTML entities)
· The fixExistingMaintenanceData() function will clean up your existing corrupted data
· Your PDF should now display completed activities correctly as: ✓ Post-planting Audit instead of & &P&o&s&t...

Just copy the two code blocks above - replace the sanitizeInput function, then run the fix function in your browser console. That should solve the problem permanently!
